<%# app/views/home/_credit_card_summary.html.erb — locals: category, summary
    The collapsed card row, unchanged in meaning: `gasto` is the statement
    payments entered this month, `orçado` is what falls due this month across
    every card — and the sum of the breakdown lines. %>
<% spent = summary.spent_cents(category) %>
<% budgeted = summary.budgeted_cents(category) %>
<%# An unbudgeted category (budgeted 0) is not an overrun — it's a category the
    user hasn't got to yet. Here `budgeted` is what falls due this month and
    `spent` is what was actually paid against statements, so this highlights
    the one case where CashForecast#card_committed switches from the due
    amount to the payment amount: the user paid more than the month's
    statements demand, e.g. settling an overdue statement from before. %>
<% over = budgeted.positive? && spent > budgeted %>
<%= link_to category.name, category_path(category, month: summary.month.strftime("%Y-%m")),
      class: "text-text hover:underline" %>
<span class="text-sm text-right block">
  <span class="<%= over ? "text-money-over font-medium" : "text-muted" %>">gasto <%= brl(spent) %> /</span>
  <span class="<%= over ? "text-money-over font-medium" : "text-muted" %>">orçado <%= brl(budgeted) %></span>
</span>
